feat(vdeploy): the _total counters survive a restart, never counted twice (GH-221) (#265)

vdeploy_plans_{started,finished,failed}_total, commits_skipped, polls,
poll_failures and head_changes reset whenever a deploy restarted the unit.
They are now totals across restarts. <state-dir>/counters.json is read once
at start as a base and rewritten atomically (temp file, fsync, rename) with
base + this run before every metrics write. The base is never added to again,
so a restart neither resets a total nor double-counts; an unreadable file is
logged and counted from zero.

Tests: a restart carries the totals over (written twice, read back, one more
plan on top); an unreadable counters.json starts from zero. vdeploy-vm
restarts the unit twice and sees exactly one more plan per restart (the
restarted agent re-plans main's tip), skipped unchanged, counters.json in
step. vdeploy-rollback-vm, vdeploy-takeover-vm and vdeploy-wake-vm green.

